# Code Quality and Refactoring Standards

## Function and Class Limits
- **Maximum 500 lines per file** - this is a hard requirement
- **Maximum 20-30 lines per function** - keep functions focused
- **Maximum 200 lines per class** - break down large classes
- **Maximum 10 methods per class** - single responsibility principle

## Refactoring Triggers
- When a file approaches 400 lines, start planning refactoring
- Extract utility functions when logic is repeated
- Create separate modules for distinct functionality
- Split large classes into smaller, focused components
- Use composition over inheritance

## Code Organization
- Group related functions together
- Separate concerns into different modules
- Use clear, descriptive file and folder names
- Maintain consistent file structure across the project
- Keep related tests close to the code they test

## Documentation
- Every public function must have JSDoc comments
- Include parameter types, return types, and examples
- Document complex algorithms and business logic
- Keep README files updated with project structure
- Use inline comments for complex logic explanations
